        },
        "texto": "The metretes, “firkin,” was the principal Greek liquid measure, and contained a little more than eight gallons and seven eighths. It corresponded to the Hebrew bath. See note on Ezekiel 45:10 (#584)."
      },
      "c-a7b341203316d4ba": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-793",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Among the Greeks, at all formal feasts, there was a “symposiarch,” who was one of the guests, and was selected to take charge of the feast. It was his duty to preserve order, to maintain liveliness among the guests, to assign each one his proper place, to decide what proportion o…"
      }
